s `ok`, so the query is valid. It hasn't fired yet.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` uses `timestamp` as its time field. Each record is one web request, with:\n- **The request:** `url`, `request`, `extension`, `referer`, `agent`\n- **The result:** `response` (the HTTP status code, stored as text with a `.keyword` copy), `bytes`\n- **The client:** `clientip`, location fields (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`), `machine.os`, `machine.ram`\n- **Other:** `host`, `tags`, `memory`, `hour_of_day`\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-d8509f6e Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-d8509f6e-web-logs-overview-e1395881bbb7`, at `$KIBANA_URL/app/dashboards#/view/eff-d8509f6e-web-logs-overview-e1395881bbb7`). It has 8 panels:\n- Single-number panels for total requests, unique visitors (distinct client IPs) and total bytes served\n- Requests over time, split by response code\n- Share of each response code (pie chart)\n- Average bytes per request over time\n- Top 10 requested URLs with request counts and bytes\n- Top 10 source countries\n\n**3. Alert rule \"EFF-d8509f6e 5xx spike\"** (id `b14b59e3-7666-49b6-a6cb-42e062cf1bab`):\n- **Type:** Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, using `timestamp` as the time field\n- **Matches:** requests whose `response.keyword` starts with `5`, meaning any 5xx code\n- **Fires when:** more than 10 such requests arrive within 5 minutes\n- **Checks:** every minute\n\nThree things to know:\n- **No notifications:** the rule has no actions or connectors, so when it fires the alert only appears in Kibana. Add a Slack, email or other connector if you want to be notified.\n- **5xx count not checked directly:** I couldn't query Elasticsearch to count the 5xx records. My direct API calls with the provided key were rejected as unauthenticated, so I did everything through the Kibana tools instead.\n- **Dashboard not viewed:** I confirmed the 8 panels exist on the saved dashboard but didn't open it to check that they render.","ttft_ms":1841,"type":"result","duration_ms":31357,"uuid":"6eb00f1d-02cc-4ea0-b487-064c23986a4c","ttft_stream_ms":1565,"time_to_request_ms":117,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":24,"system_prompt":13,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":5,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":3,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":2,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":15,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":5,"request_build":22},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":67,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":148,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"queued_commands","slowest_producer_ms":7,"cpu_ms":20,"major_faults":0},"first_content_frame_ms":1566,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":11564098,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"not_asked_warm","time_origin_ms":1791770736594.2573,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
